        "original_id": "82e6b6fa-7bcf-5198-b3f9-9e02831a2c3b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Sanming, Jiutai District, Datian County, Yinma River, Fujian, Jilin, Changchun, Yitong Manchu Autonomous County, Panshi, Dehui, Nong'an County, Kaoshan\n- Topics: Chinese administrative divisions, river geography\n\nFacts:\n- Sanming is a prefecture-level city in western Fujian province, China.\n- Jiutai District is a district under the jurisdiction of Changchun, the capital of Jilin province, China.\n- Datian County is under the jurisdiction of Sanming City.\n- The source of the Yinma River is in Yitong Manchu Autonomous County.\n- The Yinma River flows generally from south to north across Panshi, Jiutai, and Dehui.\n- The Yinma River joins the Second Songhua River at Kaoshan in Nong'an County.",
